WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:05.490
From swashbuckling swordplay to supernatural
sorcery, Netflix is a trove of hidden fantasy

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:07.700
treasures just waiting to be discovered.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:11.450
You may have seen the big titles on the streaming
service, like Pirates of the Caribbean or

00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:15.630
Stardust, but that's just the edge of the
map as far as Netflix's fantasy selection

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:16.630
is concerned.

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:20.760
We're heading into uncharted lands to seek
out the best Netflix fantasy films you should

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:22.310
be watching.

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:24.520
Legend of the Naga Pearls

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:29.270
Centuries after an ancient war between two
races, one descendant of the losing race discovers

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:33.839
a way to restore their former glory through
mystical objects known as the Naga Pearls.

00:00:33.839 --> 00:00:37.760
That's the start of the action-packed adventure
in Legend of the Naga Pearls, which sees a

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:41.909
common street thief and his CGI animal sidekick
caught in the middle of the battle to take

00:00:41.909 --> 00:00:43.730
possession of the mystical objects.

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:46.379
Whoever ends up with them could change the
fate of the world.

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:50.089
If that all sounds convoluted and ridiculous,
don't worry, it is.

00:00:50.089 --> 00:00:54.589
But it's also a ton of fun for anyone who
enjoys martial arts fantasy in all its CG-heavy,

00:00:54.589 --> 00:00:56.299
wire-fighting beauty.

00:00:56.299 --> 00:00:58.850
Cirque du Freak: The Vampire's Assistant

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:02.799
If we're all being honest with ourselves,
Cirque du Freak: The Vampire's Assistant looks

00:01:02.799 --> 00:01:03.969
downright horrible.

00:01:03.969 --> 00:01:08.479
From that overblown name to a release poster
that looks like a student film parody of Twilight,

00:01:08.479 --> 00:01:11.710
there is nothing about this movie that would
entice you to hit "play."

00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:14.399
But anyone who does give it a chance is in
for a treat.

00:01:14.399 --> 00:01:19.009
With a diverse cast that includes John C.
Reilly, Salma Hayek, Willem Dafoe, and Josh

00:01:19.009 --> 00:01:24.030
Hutcherson, The Vampire's Assistant is a bizarre
mix of fantasy, horror, and comedy that offers

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:26.719
one of the more original vampire movies of
late.

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:31.000
"Thank you ladies and gentlemen I am so excited
to be here in this anonymous small town that

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:34.420
used to have character but is now just a bland
suburb filled with chain stores and surrounded

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:36.530
by slums."

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:40.490
After two friends sneak into a traveling freak
show in their hometown, one of them becomes

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:43.659
convinced that one of the performers is a
real vampire.

00:01:43.659 --> 00:01:47.390
That fateful night leads to the two friends
joining a secret vampire war.

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:51.119
Even that description sounds terrible, but
Vampire's Assistant pulls it off well enough

00:01:51.119 --> 00:01:52.929
to make for a unique viewing experience.

00:01:52.929 --> 00:01:54.729
"Here fill that hole."

00:01:54.729 --> 00:01:56.539
"I can't do that.

00:01:56.539 --> 00:01:58.350
I'm all cramped up.

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:00.609
My legs are still numb."

00:02:00.609 --> 00:02:02.409
"Can you feel this?"

00:02:02.409 --> 00:02:03.409
"OW!"

00:02:03.409 --> 00:02:04.409
Dragonheart: Battle for the Heartfire

00:02:04.409 --> 00:02:10.190
Somehow, like the slow creep of a respiratory
infection, the 1996 fantasy adventure movie

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:13.020
Dragonheart quietly became a franchise.

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:17.190
Maybe it's because we live in a magical world,
or maybe it's just because studios love them

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:20.540
some sequels, but there are now four Dragonheart
movies.

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:25.700
"No!"

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:31.380
They all follow the same basic premise: a
dragon shares a heart with a human, and through

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:34.660
their bond they save a kingdom, or something
equally important.

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:38.140
Fortunately, you don't need to catch up on
any of the other sequels to understand what's

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:41.610
happening in 2017's Dragonheart: Battle for
the Heartfire.

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:46.620
This 2017 prequel to the original film sees
a king pass away, leaving his dragon without

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:47.620
a heart-buddy.

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:51.050
It turns out that the king had two estranged
grandchildren, though, who go to war with

00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:52.700
each other over the throne.

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:56.340
Add in Patrick Stewart as the voice behind
the dragon, and you'll be surprised just how

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:57.800
much fun you have with it.

00:02:57.800 --> 00:02:58.880
"Friends.

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:01.950
I like the sound of that."

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:04.640
Mojin: The Lost Legend

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:09.780
Equal parts archaeological adventure and supernatural
epic, Mojin: The Lost Legend follows three

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:13.990
grave robbers who are hired by a shadowy cult
leader to search for the tomb of an ancient

00:03:13.990 --> 00:03:14.990
princess.

00:03:14.990 --> 00:03:18.380
To reach the tomb, they'll have to use their
wits to make it through a series of increasingly

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:19.880
dangerous challenges.

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:23.690
You won't find many critics praising Mojin:
The Lost Legend, but don't let that steer

00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:24.690
you away.

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:28.940
While the plot may be bare-bones and the characters
fairly one-dimensional, there's a lot of fun

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:33.270
to be had in these underground catacombs as
wave after wave of supernatural terror descends

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:34.660
on our protagonists.

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:38.390
If you get a kick out of archaeologists kung
fu fighting undead demons, you're bound to

00:03:38.390 --> 00:03:40.290
have a good time with this movie.

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:41.810
Solomon Kane

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:45.920
The story of a bloodthirsty pirate who turns
to a life of peace after the devil tries to

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:51.150
claim his soul, Solomon Kane is a rare combination
of action, supernatural thrills, and fantasy

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:53.290
that doesn't get too bogged down in the spectacle.

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:59.370
"You can tell your master that I am not yet
ready for hell."

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:03.750
Kane fights hellspawn demons and regular bad
guys in equal measure, but grounds the action

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:07.210
with quieter glimpses into his own struggle
to change his ways.

00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:10.870
Critics found plenty to like about the movie,
even if audiences barely gave it a second

00:04:10.870 --> 00:04:12.210
glance.

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:14.060
The Monkey King 2

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:17.750
While the first Monkey King is enjoyable,
the sequel is where the story really comes

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:22.210
to life, following the simian deity as he
protects a traveling monk from supernatural

00:04:22.210 --> 00:04:23.210
threats.

00:04:23.210 --> 00:04:26.210
Don't get us wrong, everything about these
movies is cheesy.

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:30.151
But The Monkey King 2 loads that cheesiness
with better visuals, better pacing, and a

00:04:30.151 --> 00:04:33.950
better overall story than its predecessor,
making it a must-watch for anyone looking

00:04:33.950 --> 00:04:36.290
for a pure, unrestrained fantasy adventure.

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:40.840
And true to form for these kinds of Chinese
productions, the climactic battle is a visual

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:45.660
jumble of ridiculous CGI that alone makes
this movie worth the price of admission.

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:49.700
And since that admission price is zero to
begin with, what do you have to lose?

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:50.700
Psychokinesis

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:56.240
In just a few short years, director Yeon Sang-ho's
Train to Busan has become a modern zombie

00:04:56.240 --> 00:04:57.240
classic.

00:04:57.240 --> 00:05:02.100
With that kind of pedigree, you'd think that
his 2018 fantasy-superhero mashup Psychokinesis

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:06.240
would have made more waves, but sadly it slipped
under the current for most people.

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:10.350
When a despondent security guard unknowingly
drinks water tainted by some sort of mystical

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:14.210
meteor juice, he suddenly gains the power
to move things around with his mind.

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:18.000
With his newfound abilities, he sets out to
reconnect with his estranged daughter.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:22.580
While it takes awhile to get going, Psychokinesis
rewards viewers with an epic finale that makes

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:26.560
the whole journey worthwhile, and proves again
that Yeon is as skilled behind the camera

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:29.940
as he is at writing, heartfelt, emotional
stories.

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:32.470
Vanishing Time: A Boy Who Returned

00:05:32.470 --> 00:05:36.940
For a twisted, mind-bending fantasy experience,
look no further than Vanishing Time: A Boy

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:38.010
Who Returned.

00:05:38.010 --> 00:05:42.450
This South Korean film opens with five children
who stumble on a mysterious cave deep in the

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:45.470
forest, where they find magical egg at the
bottom of a lake.

00:05:45.470 --> 00:05:49.400
According to local legend, the egg holds a
monster that can devour time.

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:53.490
When the kids decide to break open the egg,
they unleash an unexpected supernatural force

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:55.470
that changes each and every one of them.

00:05:55.470 --> 00:05:59.760
While the central premise of Vanishing Time
has its basis in fantasy, the story that plays

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:04.500
out afterward is a remarkably gripping drama
about friendship, trust, and betrayal.

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:09.560
It's a quieter, more brutal take on the fantasy
genre, but it's just as gripping as any action-packed

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:12.210
spectacle you're likely to find on Netflix.

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:14.639
Give it a chance and you won't be disappointed.

00:06:14.639 --> 00:06:17.350
The Imaginarium of Doctor Parnassus

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:21.690
The story of a traveling troupe of performers
led by a man who's made a bet with the devil

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:25.990
to see who can collect the most souls, The
Imaginarium of Doctor Parnassus is a unique

00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:30.330
fantasy adventure that most mainstream audiences
missed in 2009.

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:35.440
Imaginarium straddles a thin line between
magical surrealism and over-the-top goofiness,

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:38.570
but to its credit, it never goes too far in
either direction.

00:06:38.570 --> 00:06:42.960
Heath Ledger does a lot to keep the film grounded,
even as it goes deeper and deeper into dreamlike

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:43.960
territory.

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:47.260
If you missed Imaginarium when it was first
released, you should definitely give it a

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:48.470
shot now that it's on Netflix.

